  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "qt6-qtbase security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for qt6-qtbase is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Qt is a software toolkit for developing applications.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the Qt QCborValue to JSON conversion of the Qt Core module.(CVE-2026-105924)\n\nOut-of-bounds read in the QAuthenticator NTLM authentication handling in the Qt Network module in Qt Group Qt allows remote attackers to obtain sensitive information (heap memory contents) or cause a denial of service (application crash) via a crafted NTLM challenge sent by a malicious server or proxy, when an application using QNetworkAccessManager or QTcpSocket authenticates with NTLM.(CVE-2026-105946)\n\nSpecially crafted CBOR input passed to QCborValue::fromCbor() in Qt Core can cause an out-of-bounds read, which may crash the application and could expose information.(CVE-2026-107157)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for qt6-qtbase is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of medium. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Medium",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "qt6-qtbase",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
